    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0247" n="127" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg127"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-01-06"><hi rendition="#italic">January 6,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 868.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith for your information a
                    copy of a note from the Chinese minister here,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d151-f1"/>
                    informing the Department that it is the decision of the Imperial Chinese
                    Government to cancel and annul the agreements made with the American China
                    Development Company, bearing date April 14, 1898, and July 13, 1900; and stating
                    the reasons; which have forced the Chinese Government to take that step.</p>
                <p>I also inclose a copy of the Department’s note to the minister, in reply.<anchor
                        n="a" xml:id="d151-f2"/></p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. B. Loomis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
